WEBVTT

00:16.485 --> 00:19.385
Taiyou ni me ga kurameba

00:19.385 --> 00:24.065
hikari no hate o shiru darou

00:24.065 --> 00:25.965
Hoshikuzu no nou

00:25.965 --> 00:31.805
Nante semai uchuu de boku wa ikiteru

00:31.805 --> 00:39.345
Dare ka zero kara hajimeru
koodo o sazukete kurenai ka

00:39.345 --> 00:41.915
Zoushoku sare sakuran

00:41.915 --> 00:45.945
Hako no naka shiseru koronii

00:45.945 --> 00:50.425
Kakan naki yume o ute

00:50.425 --> 00:53.595
Kodoku yo jibaku seyo

00:53.595 --> 00:57.995
Yubisaki no mirai ni

00:57.995 --> 01:01.835
donna sakurifaisu ga arou to

01:01.835 --> 01:05.505
Mune no oku de

01:05.505 --> 01:08.805
Kokoro koushin seyo

01:08.805 --> 01:12.945
Ippo kako no hibi ga

01:12.945 --> 01:15.945
toozakatte yukedomo

01:15.945 --> 01:23.015
Koishikarubeki kimi

01:45.875 --> 01:50.385
"A robot must obey all
orders given to it by beastmen."

01:50.385 --> 01:53.215
"A robot must always act
in the interest of beastmen."

01:53.215 --> 01:58.555
"A robot must never comply with
any order given to it by a human."

01:58.555 --> 02:05.665
I created the clockwork robots,
and I programmed them with those laws.

02:05.665 --> 02:12.725
Thus, from the robots' point of view,
I am the very god of creation!

02:15.205 --> 02:19.165
But why stop at clockwork robots?

02:19.945 --> 02:21.575
If I but had the Destruct Code...

02:21.575 --> 02:27.535
and could control its power of
destruction and creation with these hands!

02:29.785 --> 02:32.085
The Destruct Code!

02:36.025 --> 02:40.985
"There are 108 Laws of Clockwork Robotics"

02:41.765 --> 02:44.735
Hey! Look over there!

02:48.635 --> 02:51.945
Clock Town is very advanced
in terms of mechanization, bear-o.

02:51.945 --> 02:55.115
Those things are called clockwork robots...
basically mechanical dolls, bear-o.

02:55.115 --> 02:56.645
Mechanical dolls?!

02:56.645 --> 02:58.615
Wow...

02:58.615 --> 03:01.615
Hey, Morte!

03:01.615 --> 03:03.585
What's wrong now, Morte?!

03:03.585 --> 03:05.425
Why're you in such a big hurry?

03:05.425 --> 03:09.455
We didn't come here so we
could stand around watching robots.

03:09.455 --> 03:11.795
We came because the Alligator
Master is in charge of this town.

03:11.795 --> 03:15.425
And we need to ask him
about the Destruct Code.

03:16.465 --> 03:18.235
I know all that.

03:18.235 --> 03:21.275
But we're still the World Destruction Committee.

03:21.275 --> 03:24.645
Chances are we're not gonna
be able to just walk right up and ask.

03:24.645 --> 03:26.345
I thought being able to walk right up and ask...

03:26.345 --> 03:30.115
was the whole reason I had to
wear these ridiculous bunny ears again.

03:30.115 --> 03:32.515
So until we see the Alligator Master
let's not call any attention to our...

03:33.785 --> 03:34.775
Ow!

03:37.255 --> 03:40.455
Way not to call attention
to yourself there, bear-o.

03:40.455 --> 03:42.295
Hey, you alright?

03:42.295 --> 03:43.825
Clockies are smart...

03:43.825 --> 03:47.535
but even they can't get out of the way
when you ram 'em straight from behind.

03:47.535 --> 03:50.265
Hey, you travelers? Whatcha think
of the clockwork robots we got here?

03:50.265 --> 03:52.635
They're made pretty good, ain't they?

03:52.635 --> 03:55.175
They're amazingly well-made, bear-o.

03:55.175 --> 04:00.315
These guys'll do anything we ask 'em to...
I tell ya, they come in real handy!

04:00.315 --> 04:02.775
Really? Lemme try... hey, clockie!

04:02.775 --> 04:06.145
Could you grab me that
book on the ground over there?

04:08.385 --> 04:10.455
What's wrong? He busted?

04:10.455 --> 04:15.395
Hey, you! Clockwork robot over there!
Come over here and gimme a hand!

04:15.395 --> 04:16.995
Huh?

04:16.995 --> 04:21.235
It's gotta mean they follow orders
from beastmen but not from humans.

04:21.235 --> 04:23.135
Let's get outta here.

04:23.135 --> 04:25.965
Wait... are you guys?!

04:25.965 --> 04:27.495
Humans?!

04:40.755 --> 04:46.255
I must say, I never expected them
to play right into my hands like this!

04:46.255 --> 04:49.525
Some humans appear to have just entered town.

04:49.525 --> 04:52.495
Capture them. I don't care if they're injured.

04:52.495 --> 04:56.235
Additionally, two operatives claiming
to be the World Salvation Committee...

04:56.235 --> 04:58.005
are outside the tower walls.

04:58.005 --> 05:00.435
Keep those two cooling their
heels right where they are.

05:00.435 --> 05:03.745
Your top priority is to capture those humans.

05:03.745 --> 05:05.005
Understood.

05:19.625 --> 05:28.365
Welcome to Clock Town.
I will be your guide. I am at your service.

05:28.365 --> 05:32.065
That's very kind. Thank you so much. Shall we...

05:32.065 --> 05:38.445
Before we begin, I must confirm
your identities. Where are you from?

05:38.445 --> 05:42.415
We're both from the World Salvation Committee.

05:42.415 --> 05:44.885
The Hurled Salvation Crumb City?

05:44.885 --> 05:47.955
No. It's the World Salvation Committee.

05:47.955 --> 05:50.725
The Twirled Castration Bum City?

05:50.725 --> 05:53.955
That's not it... World. Salvation. Committee.

05:53.955 --> 05:57.095
The World Consternation Subcommittee?

05:57.095 --> 06:01.465
No. As I said, we're from the
World... Salvation... Committee.

06:01.465 --> 06:03.095
- You want to whirl?
You want sensation? You want a ditty?

06:03.095 --> 06:04.655
- No, that's not it.
- You want to whirl?
You want sensation? You want a ditty?

06:10.575 --> 06:14.405
Oh, no... you think they found out we're
also the World Destruction Committee?!

06:18.315 --> 06:19.745
Watch out, bear-o!

06:19.745 --> 06:22.515
These ones aren't like the
cleaning robots from before, bear-o!

06:22.515 --> 06:25.245
These are fighting robots, bear-o!

06:31.365 --> 06:33.095
Let's do this.

06:33.095 --> 06:34.925
We'll bust through the hard way!

06:45.275 --> 06:47.175
Kyrie!

06:50.785 --> 06:51.835
Ba-bear-o!

07:01.225 --> 07:02.885
Bear-o!

07:18.805 --> 07:20.575
He's calling the others!

07:20.575 --> 07:22.305
Stop it, bear-o!

07:23.575 --> 07:26.075
As you wish.

07:29.155 --> 07:35.825
Of course... Toppy, you're a
beastman, so they'll obey you!

07:35.825 --> 07:39.765
For now, take us someplace where
there's no one else around, bear-o!

07:39.765 --> 07:42.095
Understood. Follow me.

07:46.505 --> 07:47.935
What?

07:48.705 --> 07:51.045
You're saying they escaped?!

07:51.045 --> 07:54.345
Yes. It appears that one of the
clockwork robots has inadvertently...

07:54.345 --> 07:59.945
complied with an order from the
beastman in the World Destruction Committee.

07:59.945 --> 08:01.185
How can that be?!

08:01.185 --> 08:02.685
As a special countermeasure
against the World Destruction Committee...

08:02.685 --> 08:05.425
I specifically added a supplemental
condition to the Clockwork Laws...

08:05.425 --> 08:09.055
stipulating that robots were not to
take orders from the beastman Bear tribe.

08:09.055 --> 08:12.765
The condition should have been in effect!

08:12.765 --> 08:14.395
It appears that the target
was not from the Bear tribe...

08:14.395 --> 08:16.695
but from the Little Bear tribe.

08:16.695 --> 08:17.965
What was that?!

08:17.965 --> 08:22.465
In that case, the pictures on this
wanted poster must be incorrect!

08:30.315 --> 08:34.955
What shall I do now, Master Little
Bear? I await your next command.

08:34.955 --> 08:36.785
Don't call me a bear, bear-o.

08:36.785 --> 08:39.055
As you wish.

08:39.055 --> 08:42.655
What do we do now? We've come all this way...

08:48.165 --> 08:50.465
Take us to the Alligator Master.

08:50.465 --> 08:52.765
According to the
Third Law of Clockwork Robotics...

08:52.765 --> 08:56.565
I cannot comply with any
order given to me by a human.

08:57.575 --> 08:59.075
Toppy.

08:59.075 --> 09:00.475
It's too dangerous, bear-o!

09:00.475 --> 09:03.675
Ask me again after you've
come up with a different plan, bear-o.

09:06.615 --> 09:08.345
Wait, Morte!

09:11.525 --> 09:13.255
They found us!

09:14.925 --> 09:17.695
Toppy, order them down.

09:17.695 --> 09:21.295
All of you! Make way for us, bear-o!

09:21.295 --> 09:23.925
What's the problem?! That's an order, bear-o!

09:24.965 --> 09:29.775
It appears that the programming for
the Clockwork Laws has been rewritten.

09:29.775 --> 09:31.605
Wh-What are we gonna do?!

09:31.605 --> 09:33.975
Morte and I will open up a path, bear-o!

09:33.975 --> 09:36.515
While we're doing that, you run, bear-o!

09:36.515 --> 09:40.785
N-N-No, I'm f-fine.
I can help a little too, I think...

09:40.785 --> 09:44.525
Toppy! Keep it safe!

09:44.525 --> 09:46.855
I will come back for you, bear-o!

09:47.855 --> 09:50.895
B-B-But, Morte! What're you doing?!

09:50.895 --> 09:53.225
I'm doing this.

09:55.965 --> 09:58.835
This way we get to meet the
Alligator Master no matter what.

09:58.835 --> 10:01.335
So the Alligator Master's
gotta be a pretty nice guy, right?

10:01.335 --> 10:02.635
Beats me.

10:16.585 --> 10:19.425
The Pearl Starvation Nitty-Gritty?

10:19.425 --> 10:25.325
No, like I said...
the Wor-Id Sal-va-tion Com-mit-tee.

10:27.095 --> 10:28.395
Lia?

10:38.945 --> 10:42.075
We won't get anything done if we
keep standing around here, bear-o!

10:42.075 --> 10:45.045
Do you know where the two
of them were taken, bear-o?

10:45.045 --> 10:46.345
Yes I do.

10:46.345 --> 10:47.885
Then where, bear-o?!

10:47.885 --> 10:53.055
The tallest tower in that direction is
the Alligator Master's Clock Fortress.

10:53.055 --> 10:55.295
The two humans are inside.

10:55.295 --> 10:57.455
All right, show me there, bear-o!

11:04.205 --> 11:08.035
So you two are the
World Destruction Committee?

11:08.035 --> 11:10.035
And you must be the Alligator Master.

11:10.035 --> 11:12.875
Sorry to skip the formalities, but
there's something I want to ask you about.

11:12.875 --> 11:15.415
Be mindful of your position.

11:15.415 --> 11:19.485
I believe that I am the one who
has the right to ask the questions here...

11:19.485 --> 11:22.585
given the situation as it stands.

11:22.585 --> 11:26.755
But very well... I will deign
to answer your question.

11:26.755 --> 11:32.285
What you want to know is how to
use the Destruct Code, isn't that right?

11:34.065 --> 11:35.735
Are you some kind of fool?

11:35.735 --> 11:39.235
Here you are, attempting to wreak
destruction upon beastmen such as myself...

11:39.235 --> 11:43.175
and you honestly expect me to tell
you how to use the Destruct Code?!

11:43.175 --> 11:46.505
I must say, you do amuse me, little girl.

11:46.505 --> 11:49.575
But do you even know
what it is that you're asking?

11:49.575 --> 11:55.355
The Destruct Code isn't some secret
weapon for you to use to defeat us beastmen.

11:55.355 --> 11:57.925
If you activate the Destruct Code...

11:57.925 --> 12:01.855
then just as the legends say, the
whole world will return to elemental sand.

12:01.855 --> 12:06.125
And both you and I will vanish
from this world without a trace.

12:06.125 --> 12:11.465
Your so-called
"world destruction" is precisely that.

12:11.465 --> 12:14.025
That's fine by me.

12:16.935 --> 12:19.645
I'm from the World Salvation Committee.

12:19.645 --> 12:21.945
The Curled Crustacean Drum Kitty?

12:21.945 --> 12:25.685
That's right... I'm from the
Curled Crustacean Drum Kitty.

12:25.685 --> 12:27.655
Now please show me to the Alligator Master.

12:27.655 --> 12:32.845
No kitty known as the "Curled
Crustacean Drum Kitty" exists in my databa...

12:43.695 --> 12:45.165
The way is up. We go up.

12:45.165 --> 12:46.905
W-W-W-W-Wait just a minute, bear-o!

12:46.905 --> 12:48.875
Stop it! Stop pushing me, bear-o!

12:48.875 --> 12:51.705
Bear-oooooo!

12:59.345 --> 13:01.055
What's wrong, bear-o?

13:01.055 --> 13:03.415
I have overheated.

13:05.255 --> 13:08.725
Well, don't push it, bear-o!
Just rest a bit, bear-o.

13:08.725 --> 13:10.865
I will do as you ask.

13:10.865 --> 13:14.335
By the way, I never asked you your name, bear-o.

13:14.335 --> 13:16.265
I have no name.

13:16.265 --> 13:21.405
If you must distinguish me from
other robots, please call me Number 28.

13:21.405 --> 13:23.005
Number 28?

13:23.005 --> 13:25.675
That is my serial number.

13:25.675 --> 13:28.745
I have now cooled down. Let us proceed.

13:28.745 --> 13:31.505
B-But w-wait! I need
time to mentally prepare!

13:34.585 --> 13:36.285
That's fine by you?!

13:36.285 --> 13:39.855
You may be fine with it, but what
about the young man standing beside you?

13:39.855 --> 13:43.055
He certainly doesn't seem to be on
board with this so-called plan of yours.

13:43.055 --> 13:44.455
Yea...!

13:46.795 --> 13:50.195
Well, I've spent quite enough time
humoring you with this little diversion.

13:50.195 --> 13:54.135
Now it's time for you
to hand over the Destruct Code!

13:54.135 --> 13:55.735
I don't have it here.

13:55.735 --> 14:01.415
Lying won't do you any good.
Take a look at that machine over there!

14:01.415 --> 14:05.285
What you see there is
the Destruct Code Detector.

14:05.285 --> 14:05.945
Many years ago...

14:05.945 --> 14:09.655
that is to say, perhaps thousands
or even tens of thousands of years ago...

14:09.655 --> 14:11.985
when the Destruct Code activated...

14:11.985 --> 14:15.795
it left behind some residual energy,
which I analyzed and used to create this.

14:15.795 --> 14:18.495
Unfortunately, since I was
unable to miniaturize it any further...

14:18.495 --> 14:21.395
the detector could not fully
fulfill its intended purpose.

14:21.395 --> 14:24.505
But take a look at that light!

14:24.505 --> 14:27.465
It means the Destruct Code is close by!

14:30.275 --> 14:33.505
So then... produce the Destruct Code at once.

14:33.505 --> 14:36.645
Didn't you hear me? I said I don't have it.

14:36.645 --> 14:39.315
You must be hiding it somewhere.

14:39.315 --> 14:42.405
Find it, even if it means
tearing them limb from limb!

14:59.005 --> 15:00.775
Number 28!

15:00.775 --> 15:03.605
Help the two of them escape, bear-o!

15:05.705 --> 15:08.615
Cease at once. Cease all violence at once.

15:08.615 --> 15:11.015
Out of my way, you buckets of bolts!

15:12.385 --> 15:16.185
Say your prayers, World Destruction Committee!

15:26.225 --> 15:30.025
Y-You fool! Don't shoot at the detector!

15:39.705 --> 15:41.145
Bear-o!

15:52.185 --> 15:54.815
It's resonating!

16:06.435 --> 16:08.025
What is this?!

16:09.105 --> 16:11.675
Dragon Valley...

16:11.675 --> 16:16.415
This landscape is indeed that of
Dragon Valley on the winter continent.

16:16.415 --> 16:19.215
But why has it appeared?

16:24.625 --> 16:27.385
So this thing showed it to us!

16:39.465 --> 16:41.935
Now let us run away.

16:42.935 --> 16:44.765
Don't let them get away!

17:07.225 --> 17:13.135
You are in danger. Please run
away at once. Do not worry about me.

17:18.775 --> 17:20.575
Thank you very much.

17:20.575 --> 17:23.735
Forget about thanking me...
let's just get out of here, bear-o!

17:26.245 --> 17:27.855
Sorry I'm late...

17:27.855 --> 17:30.485
You wouldn't believe how much time it took...

17:30.485 --> 17:34.125
to finally get our correct identity
through to those clockwork robots.

17:34.125 --> 17:35.855
What's wrong?

17:35.855 --> 17:38.095
Oh... uh, nothing.

17:38.095 --> 17:41.765
I did manage to locate those
World Destruction Committee guys...

17:41.765 --> 17:44.365
but somehow I let them slip away again.

17:44.365 --> 17:49.325
Still, they can't have
gone too far yet. Let's go.

17:52.475 --> 17:54.175
What is it this time?

17:54.175 --> 17:59.375
It would seem the World Salvation
Committee just isn't welcome here.

18:01.955 --> 18:03.285
Are you all right, bear-o?

18:03.285 --> 18:06.685
The damage to me is inconsequential. However...

18:06.685 --> 18:08.895
"However"? What is it, bear-o?

18:08.895 --> 18:11.895
Why did you rescue me?

18:11.895 --> 18:17.335
Do the Laws of Beastmen have a
clause about protecting clockwork robots?

18:17.335 --> 18:19.365
No, there's nothing like that, bear-o.

18:19.365 --> 18:21.405
In that case, why?

18:21.405 --> 18:23.835
It does not compute.

18:23.835 --> 18:27.475
That's the difference between
clockwork robots and living things, bear-o.

18:27.475 --> 18:30.875
We don't have any
predefined set of rules, bear-o.

18:30.875 --> 18:33.345
We make our own decisions.

18:33.345 --> 18:35.755
It's what we call a "soul," bear-o.

18:35.755 --> 18:38.215
A soul?

18:47.565 --> 18:50.085
This is as far as you go.

18:51.435 --> 18:55.405
Now then... it's time for you
to hand that thing over to me.

18:55.405 --> 18:59.405
You will obey my command!

18:59.405 --> 19:01.545
Number 28! Don't do it, bear-o!

19:01.545 --> 19:04.015
Don't listen to what he says, bear-o!

19:04.945 --> 19:06.415
Number 28!

19:08.915 --> 19:11.185
There's nothing to compute here.

19:11.185 --> 19:14.425
Now, I grant you special
authorization to use your gun.

19:14.425 --> 19:15.855
Engage!

19:24.035 --> 19:26.295
Don't do it, bear-o!

19:38.615 --> 19:40.945
Let us run away. The way is up.

19:40.945 --> 19:42.315
What'd you just say?!

19:51.325 --> 19:54.595
It's no good! They're catching up to us!

19:58.005 --> 20:00.005
Number 28!

20:00.005 --> 20:05.475
You must not approach.
Please run away and leave this to me.

20:05.475 --> 20:07.675
I can't do that, bear-o!

20:07.675 --> 20:09.835
Please run away.

20:11.615 --> 20:13.305
Number 28!

20:17.655 --> 20:20.485
Number 28!

20:42.945 --> 20:46.315
It won't do you any good
to keep dwelling on it like this.

20:46.315 --> 20:49.685
Oh, I forgot... Toppy,
do you have the Destruct Code?

20:49.685 --> 20:52.355
Number 28 still had it on him, bear-o!

20:52.355 --> 20:55.055
Eh?! What was that?!

20:55.695 --> 20:59.325
We can't go back, Morte!
We just barely managed to get away!

20:59.325 --> 21:00.295
Hey, let go of me!

21:00.295 --> 21:01.865
Morte! We can't, bear-o!

21:01.865 --> 21:03.465
What is the problem?

21:03.465 --> 21:04.335
Bear-o!

21:04.335 --> 21:05.565
Number 28!

21:05.565 --> 21:08.165
He's still alive!

21:08.875 --> 21:10.705
You left this behind.

21:10.705 --> 21:13.505
Number 28, I'm so glad you're safe, bear-o!

21:13.505 --> 21:17.645
Of course I am. The 107th
Law of Clockwork Robotics states...

21:17.645 --> 21:22.055
"A clockwork robot must
protect its own existence."

21:22.055 --> 21:24.385
I await your next command.

21:24.385 --> 21:26.725
I have no more commands, bear-o.

21:26.725 --> 21:29.985
Master Toppy, please issue a command.

21:31.725 --> 21:33.865
Then return to Clock Town, bear-o.

21:33.865 --> 21:38.565
And once there, live your life
the way you want to live it, bear-o.

21:38.565 --> 21:44.365
Live... that is a very difficult
theoretical concept, but I will try.

21:45.105 --> 21:47.045
Farewell, bear-o!

21:56.115 --> 21:57.115
Let's get going.

21:57.115 --> 21:58.425
"Going"?

21:58.425 --> 22:00.925
So we don't need to do anything
more with the Alligator Master's book?

22:00.925 --> 22:04.595
Nope. Now let's get going
before they start coming after us.

22:04.595 --> 22:06.285
Morte!

22:07.695 --> 22:13.535
They'll be heading for
Dragon Valley on the winter continent.

22:14.135 --> 22:18.535
And the Destruct Code will be mine!

22:21.105 --> 22:24.615
Kirameku suna no umi

22:24.615 --> 22:27.745
Aoi chijou no hate

22:27.745 --> 22:33.825
Yuuyami ni ochita sora kara

22:33.825 --> 22:36.955
afuredasu kioku

22:36.955 --> 22:40.165
Gareki no you ni

22:40.165 --> 22:46.165
kasanete yuku darou

22:46.165 --> 22:49.405
Meguriau inochi

22:49.405 --> 22:52.475
Surechigau kimochi

22:52.475 --> 22:55.615
Tsumugiau kotoba

22:55.615 --> 22:58.745
Kizutsukeau mono

22:58.745 --> 23:10.855
Sore demo bokura ga aruiteku
michi wa asu e tsuzuiteru no

23:13.695 --> 23:17.535
Ima o against the world ikiru imi wa

23:17.535 --> 23:20.535
change the world hitotsu janai

23:20.535 --> 23:26.105
Namima no mukou haruka na tabi e

23:26.105 --> 23:29.675
Dakara around the world ikiru kodou

23:29.675 --> 23:33.215
To the end of the world kaze ni hibike

23:33.215 --> 23:39.185
Sono saki ni aru

23:39.185 --> 23:50.795
yakusoku no chi, tadoritsukeru made

23:52.735 --> 23:55.035
Having made our escape from Clock Town...

23:55.035 --> 23:59.075
the three of us headed for the winter
continent, guided by the Destruct Code.

23:59.075 --> 24:02.845
And what we found awaiting us there,
in ice-covered Dragon Valley...

24:02.845 --> 24:05.585
was the final descendant of the Dragon tribe.

24:05.585 --> 24:08.485
Next time on World Destruction... Episode 11:

24:08.485 --> 24:10.215
"There Are Two Kinds of Power."

24:10.215 --> 24:14.485
T-T-T-T-T-T-Toppy, you can't!
If you fall asleep here, you'll freeze to death!

24:14.485 --> 24:16.895
I'm a bear, so I'll be fine, bear-o...

24:16.895 --> 24:20.025
So you're admitting
you're a bear, huh? ...Bear-o?

24:20.025 --> 24:20.925
Oops.
